      "designation_data": {
        "citation": "(541132) Lele&#257;k&#363;honua = 2015 TG387<br><br>Lele&#257;k&#363;honua is a life form mentioned in the Hawaiian creation chant, the Kumulipo.  The name compares the orbit to the flight of migratory birds and evokes a yearning to be near Earth. Me he manu i ke ala p&#333;`aiapuni l&#257;, he pa`a mau n&#333; ia i ka hui me kona p&#363;nana i kumu mai ai. ",
